\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Minima $a^{*}$ of $f(a)$ for different configurations of $\ensuremath  {\mathbb  {F}}$ (of characteristic $q$ and and degree $d$ over its prime field), witness sizes $\ell $, and $\tau $ such that $\ell _1=\ell ^\tau $. By choosing primes in the interval $[2^{a^*}, 2^{128-r_1}]$, we have that the first error term $\kappa _0$ satisfies $\kappa _0 \lessapprox f(a^*)$. We include the bits left required to achieve $\kappa _0 < 1/2^{128}$ and the cost of grinding such amount of bits, in a MacBook Air M4 16GB, multi-threaded, using Blake3 as hash function. We omit configurations whose grinding cost exceeds $\approx 250$ms; in particular $\tau =0.6$ is omitted for larger $\ell $.}}{41}{table.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
